{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-09-Jul-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A tangent is drawn from a point that is at a distance of 37 cm from center of the circle O, and diameter is 24 cm. The length (in cm) of the tangent is:", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "28.16", "added": false}, {"text": "37", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The lines x+y = 10 and -3x+y = 2 have a unique solution. What is the distance (in units) between the unique solution and the point of intersection of the line x+y = 10 and the x-axis?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "An amount invested fetched a total simple interest of ₹4,050 at the rate of 9% per annum in 5 years. What is the amount invested (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "9,000", "added": false}, {"text": "8,300", "added": false}, {"text": "7,500", "added": false}, {"text": "9,050", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "If 6 engineers can complete a work in 5 days and 5 skilled workers can complete the same work in 7 days, then the time taken (in days) to complete the same work by 7 engineers and 4 skilled workers will be:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "efficiency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5175", "added": false}, {"text": "9000", "added": false}, {"text": "2250", "added": false}, {"text": "1575", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "If Tanya walks at the speed of 6 km/h, she misses a train by 2 minutes. However, if she walks at the speed of 8 km/h, she reaches the station 3 minutes before the arrival of the train. The distance covered by Tanya to reach the station is:", "options": [{"text": "3 km", "added": false}, {"text": "2.5 km", "added": false}, {"text": "2.75 km", "added": false}, {"text": "2 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "early-late", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Find the equation of the sphere having centre (-1,2,-3) and the radius of 3 units.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "If a person’s salary increases from ₹200 per day to ₹234 per day, then the percentage increase in the person’s salary is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "81.25", "added": false}, {"text": "84.5", "added": false}, {"text": "62.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The area of three adjacent faces of a cuboidal box is 120 cm2, 72 cm2 and 60 cm2, respectively. Find the volume (in cm3) of the box.", "options": [{"text": "425", "added": false}, {"text": "650", "added": false}, {"text": "720", "added": false}, {"text": "864", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "If the radius of the base and slant height of the cone is 6 cm and 10 cm, respectively, then the volume of the cone is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "98 π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "106 π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "96π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "108 π cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "In an election there were only two candidates. One of the candidates secured 35% of votes and is defeated by the other candidate by 381 votes. The total number of votes polled is:", "options": [{"text": "635", "added": false}, {"text": "1028", "added": false}, {"text": "1270", "added": false}, {"text": "514", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "In a right angle triangle with sides 12 cm and 16 cm and hypotenuse 20 cm, the length of altitude drawn on the hypotenuse from the opposite vertex is K. Find the value of K.", "options": [{"text": "6.9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9.6 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6.8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8.6cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}